# Measurement only. Deliberately NOT in requirements.in: the font build must
# stay reproducible and lean, and a clone should be able to build the family
# without any of this.
#
# These exist because four hand-written gauges in a row measured a model of the
# glyph rather than the glyph, and each reported a confident wrong number --
# see docs/METHOD.md F11. Where a mature library does the job, use it.
#
#   scipy         exact Euclidean distance transform (the stroke-weight
#                 reading) and enclosed-region fill (counters), both in C
#   scikit-image  medial_axis: a centreline and its half-width in one call,
#                 as an independent second opinion on the centreline this
#                 project derives from the contours
#   shapely       a correct, well-tested offsetter, used to CHECK that a
#                 re-stroked centreline came out where it should
#   pytest        so the instrument's self-test is a test rather than a
#                 script nobody re-runs

scipy>=1.11
scikit-image>=0.22
shapely>=2.0
pytest>=8.0
